<title>SWEDEN: Scania says staff cuts to hit Q4.</title>
<headline>Scania says staff cuts to hit Q4.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish truck and bus maker Scania on Thursday said a staff reduction programme would hit fourth quarter profits by around 300 million crowns.</p>
<p>&quot;To continue a staff reduction programme, as earlier announced, a programme will be introduced that is estimated to burden the fourth quarter by about 300 million crowns,&quot; Scania said in it report for the first nine months of 1996.</p>
<p>Scania said in the first nine months of the year it cut European production staff by 750 through natural wastage and by not renewing temporary contracts.</p>
<p>During the period the total number of employees internationally fell to 22,340, a reduction of 780 people on a year ago.</p>
<p>-- STockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
